#: src/Admin/HelpDocumentationPage.php:179
msgid "Open your sitemap index in a browser to see a readable overview. The top explains what the file is and gives you the one address to submit, with copy and Search Console shortcuts. Below it, a short three-step strip explains how sitemaps work, four totals show how many addresses, content types and files are listed and when the newest change happened, and the “What’s in your sitemap” list shows one row per content type with its icon, a plain description, the number of addresses, its share of the total and when it last changed. An empty row is normal: it fills up automatically when matching content is published. Open a row to see every address in that file, with filtering, paging and quick checks (URL limit, last-modified dates, HTTPS and news data). Search engines never use this view; they read the plain XML. Use View raw XML to see exactly what crawlers receive. Very large indexes skip per-file URL counts to stay fast."
